WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.760
In this lesson, you will learn to use the timer and counters to limit time, increase difficulty as the game goes on, and end the game cleanly.

2
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.960
A countdown variable starts at a number and goes down by 1 every second.

3
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.930
When it reaches 0, the game ends.

4
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:21.770
Store the speed in a variable and increase it over time.

5
00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:29.010
Use the variable in the movement block so everything speeds up.

6
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.880
When lives reach 0 or time runs out: show the final score and stop all.

7
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.570
A clear ending makes a game feel finished.

8
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.490
Start easy, get harder gradually.

9
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:43.220
Players should feel “I almost made it — one more go!”

10
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.910
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

11
00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:51.690
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
